{
  "name": "How to Prepare for a Roof Wear-and-Tear Assessment",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1: Gather Roof History — Before we arrive, try to pull together any information you have on your roof’s age, when it was last replaced or significantly repaired, and any warranty details you might have. Knowing this helps us understand its baseline and history of any past issues.",
      "text": "Step 1: Gather Roof History — Before we arrive, try to pull together any information you have on your roof’s age, when it was last replaced or significantly repaired, and any warranty details you might have. Knowing this helps us understand its baseline and history of any past issues.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 2: Note Any Concerns — Walk around your property and inside your attic if it's safe to do so. Make a quick list of anything you've noticed—leaks, stains, missing shingles, strange sounds, or even just areas that look a bit off. This helps us focus on potential problem spots right away.",
      "text": "Step 2: Note Any Concerns — Walk around your property and inside your attic if it's safe to do so. Make a quick list of anything you've noticed—leaks, stains, missing shingles, strange sounds, or even just areas that look a bit off. This helps us focus on potential problem spots right away.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 2
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 3: Clear the Perimeter — Ensure clear access around your home. Trim any overgrown bushes or trees that are directly against the house and move any vehicles or outdoor furniture that might obstruct the ladder placement or our ability to walk around the exterior. This ensures our team can safely and efficiently inspect all areas.",
      "text": "Step 3: Clear the Perimeter — Ensure clear access around your home. Trim any overgrown bushes or trees that are directly against the house and move any vehicles or outdoor furniture that might obstruct the ladder placement or our ability to walk around the exterior. This ensures our team can safely and efficiently inspect all areas.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 4: Secure Pets and Valuables — On the day of the assessment, make sure your pets are secured indoors or in a safe area away from the work zone. If you have any delicate plants or valuables directly beneath the roofline, consider moving them just in case. Safety is always our top priority.",
      "text": "Step 4: Secure Pets and Valuables — On the day of the assessment, make sure your pets are secured indoors or in a safe area away from the work zone. If you have any delicate plants or valuables directly beneath the roofline, consider moving them just in case. Safety is always our top priority.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 4
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 5: Be Available for Questions — Our team will likely have a few questions for you during the inspection, especially regarding any past issues or future plans for your home. Being available to chat for a few minutes can help us provide the most comprehensive assessment.",
      "text": "Ready to get started? Contact Discounted Roofing Co. today to schedule your wear-and-tear assessment and we’ll guide you step by step.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 5
    }
  ],
